  "description": "A merchant brigantine found adrift, empty, and unexplained.\n\nThe mystery has spurred countless theories, from piracy to supernatural.\n\nKey points:\n- Discovered December 1872 off the Azores\n- No crew, intact cargo, lifeboat missing\n- No evidence of foul play, yet mystery endures\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Mary Celeste\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Celeste), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nGonave.jpg (NASA, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gonave.jpg\nMary Celeste NYTimes 1873February26.png (Boston Post, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mary_Celeste_NYTimes_1873February26.png\nLap desk of Captain Benjamin Briggs from the Mary Celeste (PEM M6557) 02.jpg (Crawdad Blues, CC0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lap_desk_of_Captain_Benjamin_Briggs_from_the_Mary_Celeste_(PEM_M6557)_02.jpg\nArthur Conan Doyle by Herbert Rose Barraud 1893.jpg (Herbert Rose Barraud (1845 - c1896), Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arthur_Conan_Doyle_by_Herbert_Rose_Barraud_1893.jpg\nVillageview.jpg (Dan Conlin, CC BY-SA 3.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Villageview.jpg\nMary Celeste as Amazon in 1861 (cropped).jpg (Unconfirmed, possibly Honore Pellegrin (1800 – c.1870). This speculative attribu, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mary_Celeste_as_Amazon_in_1861_(cropped).jpg",
